---
import DesktopLayout from '../../layouts/DesktopLayout.astro';
const sections=[['guides','Desktop guides'],['install','Installing Desktop'],['windows-unsigned','Windows SmartScreen'],['macos-open-anyway','Opening on macOS'],['trial','Trial and activation'],['license-email','License email'],['replace-device','Replacing a device'],['promo-codes','Promo codes']];
const guides=[['what-is-sorafiles-desktop','What is SoraFiles Desktop?'],['how-sorafiles-desktop-works','How SoraFiles Desktop works'],['getting-started-with-sorafiles-desktop','Getting started with SoraFiles Desktop'],['use-sorafiles-from-your-file-manager','Use SoraFiles from your file manager'],['sorafiles-web-vs-desktop','SoraFiles Web vs Desktop'],['using-sorafiles-desktop-offline','Using SoraFiles Desktop offline']];
---
<DesktopLayout title="SoraFiles Desktop help" description="Installation, activation and platform guidance for SoraFiles Desktop." path="/desktop/help">
 <div class="dw-container"><header class="dw-intro"><h1>Desktop help</h1></header><div class="dw-doc-layout"><nav class="dw-toc" aria-label="On this page"><strong>On this page</strong>{sections.map(([id,label])=><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a>)}</nav><div class="dw-doc-content">
  <section id="guides"><h2>Desktop guides</h2><p>New to Desktop? Start here.</p><ul class="guide-links">{guides.map(([slug,title])=><li><a class="dw-link" href={`/guides/${slug}`}>{title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>)}</ul></section>
  <section id="install"><h2>Installing Desktop</h2><p>Download the installer for your operating system from <a href="/desktop/download" class="dw-link">Downloads</a>. Verify its published SHA-256 checksum before opening it. Desktop does not update itself automatically.</p><p>On Linux, install the DEB package or allow the AppImage to run as a program. Available packages and supported operating systems are listed with each download.</p></section>
  <section id="windows-unsigned"><h2>Windows SmartScreen</h2><p>The current Windows installer is unsigned, so Microsoft Defender SmartScreen may say that Windows protected your PC. After verifying the SHA-256 checksum and confirming that you downloaded the installer from the SoraFiles release page, select <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>.</p><p>A publisher warning may continue until SoraFiles ships a certificate-signed installer.</p></section>
  <section id="macos-open-anyway"><h2>Opening SoraFiles on macOS</h2><p>Current Mac builds are ad-hoc signed and are not notarized by Apple. If macOS blocks the first launch, use these steps for a SoraFiles download you trust:</p><ol><li>Open the DMG, drag SoraFiles Desktop to Applications, then try opening it once.</li><li>Open System Settings, select Privacy &amp; Security, and scroll to the message about SoraFiles Desktop.</li><li>Select Open Anyway, then confirm Open when prompted.</li></ol><p>This approves the app on this Mac; it does not notarize it. If macOS reports that the app is damaged or will harm your computer, do not override that alert. See <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102445" class="dw-link">Apple’s opening instructions</a>.</p></section>
  <section id="trial"><h2>Trial and activation</h2><p>Your free 7-day trial begins automatically when you first open SoraFiles Desktop on Windows, macOS or Linux. Connect to the internet to finish trial setup; waiting to connect does not extend the trial.</p><p>To continue after the trial, choose License → Activate License and paste the key from your purchase email. File processing works offline after setup. Setup, activation and subscription renewals need an internet connection. A Lifetime license continues to work offline after activation.</p></section>
  <section id="license-email"><h2>Can’t find your license email?</h2><p>Check the inbox for the email address used at checkout, including <strong>Spam or Junk</strong>. Look for “Your License Key is Ready” from <span class="sender">noreply@dodopayments.com</span>. If it landed in Spam, mark it as not spam.</p><p>If you still cannot find it, <a href="/contact" class="dw-link">contact us</a> for help.</p></section>
  <section id="replace-device"><h2>Replacing a device</h2><p>Open License → Replace device in SoraFiles Desktop. Verify your purchaser email, then continue to the one-time replacement checkout. The exact fee appears before payment.</p><p>An unused Team seat activates without a replacement fee.</p><table class="dw-table"><caption>One-time device replacement fees · USD</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Personal</th><th scope="col">Team, per occupied seat</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[['Monthly','$0.99','$3.99'],['Annual','$9.99','$39.99'],['Lifetime','$49.99','$199.99']].map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row[0]}</th><td>{row[1]}</td><td>{row[2]}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p>Replacement fees are fixed and cannot be discounted. Start replacement inside Desktop; verifying the purchaser email is required before payment.</p></section>
  <section id="promo-codes"><h2>Where do I enter a promo code?</h2><p>Enter a discount code at checkout before payment. An invitation to receive a license is separate: follow its instructions on the <a href="/desktop/redeem" class="dw-link">redemption page</a>.</p><p>SoraFiles Web remains free. <a href="/tools" class="dw-link">Open the web tools</a> without a Desktop purchase.</p></section>
 </div></div></div>
</DesktopLayout>
<style>.guide-links{list-style:none;display:grid;gap:0;margin-top:16px}.guide-links li{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin:0!important}.guide-links a{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;padding:12px 0;font-size:14px;text-decoration:none}.guide-links a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.dw-doc-content p{font-size:15px}.dw-doc-content caption{text-align:left;font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-secondary);padding:16px 0}.sender{overflow-wrap:anywhere}</style>
